{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Command Handler.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Command Handler.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"command handler command handler","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Command Handler.md","fileName":"Command Handler.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Command Handler","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Application Commands and Service Boundaries]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Application Commands and Service Boundaries","Application Command","Aggregate","Single Responsibility Principle","Application Service","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Command Handler.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Command Handler.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"command handler command handler","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Command Handler.md","fileName":"Command Handler.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Command Handler","heading":"Command Handler","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A command handler is a class or function dedicated to one [[Application Command]] type. It loads or creates the relevant [[Aggregate]], invokes domain behavior, and coordinates persistence. One handler per command supports the [[Single Responsibility Principle]] and makes dependencies explicit, but a large API can create many injected handlers. An [[Application Service]] is an alternative grouping when several related commands share coordination needs; neither pattern is universally superior.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Application Commands and Service Boundaries","Application Command","Aggregate","Single Responsibility Principle","Application Service","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 -